  "title": "2026 Midseason Report",
  "intro": [
    "Welcome to the 2026 midseason report, otherwise known as the Week 8 recap with a lot more tables. It’s been a slow year for some teams, but none of them were as slow as Kramer’s New York City Marathon time this past weekend. (He was running at his girlfriend’s pace, guys. I swear.) We’ve got midseason grades, playoff odds, player analytics and a few awards that probably won’t be making anyone’s résumé."
  ],
  "lead": {
    "title": "Week 8",
    "body": [
      "New England Keys scored **193.90** and beat It Hurts When I Pitts by **125.84**, setting regular-season league records for points and winning margin. Joe Burrow and Tee Higgins combined for 74.98, enough to beat the opposing ten-man lineup themselves. The previous scoring record was 187.61, set by the franchise now called Hanging With Hernandez in Week 2 last season.",
      "Woody’s Toy Box had a less enjoyable Sunday. Bhayshul Tuten and Tony Pollard supplied 56.10 points; the team scored 132.65 and lost by 5.91. **New York Mudbones scored 138.56, their lowest total all season.** It was second-highest in Week 8.",
      "Chris Renna managed **60.24**, the lowest score by anyone other than Dackerly since the league began. Dackerly's 94.98 was ninth this week after seven straight last-place finishes. The weekly $10 charge has a new recipient."
    ]
  },
